{
  "case_id": "2019-19-431",
  "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nGEN. NOEL J. FRANCISCO, Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners in 19-454.\nPAUL D. CLEMENT, Esquire, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner in 19-431.\nMICHAEL J. FISCHER, Chief Deputy Attorney General, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Noel J. Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, RFRA at the very least authorizes the religious exemption. It prohibits the government from imposing a substantial burden on religious beliefs subject to a discretionary exception."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government (General FRANCISCO)",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I was focusing on Ricci against DeStefano, which I think gives the government flexibility when it's facing potentially competing obligations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Clement, the -- the -- I'd like you to have an opportunity to comment on the questionable standing of the states in this case, as well as the proliferation of national -- nationwide injunctions, such as the one in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Clement. I'd like to start by asking you about a -- a response that you gave to the Chief Justice, because you said there that you had no objection to objecting, the Little Sisters didn't, and I've taken that to be your consistent position throughout the litigation. But what if an employer did have an objection to objecting? In other words, had an even more, say, extended under --view of complicity so that he thought that -- the employer thought that extending itself made him"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0002-0006",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "a major feature of the opinion below and the arguments in the briefs at least was that the government had failed to comply with the procedural requirements of the APA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0002-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government, I think, on this record has complied with all of the textual requirements of the APA procedurally, and yet they've still been found to -- to be out of compliance based on an atextual test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Clement. I want to follow up on Justice Kagan's question about the objection to objecting. I had thought that would be litigated, thought out under the least restrictive alternative prong of RFRA, and the government might be able to argue that there's no less restrictive alternative available in that situation. You might disagree and try to identify a less restrictive alternative, but I had thought that's where it would be litigated. Is that correct or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was a hypothetical in one of the amicus briefs that I thought was pretty good and I haven't heard an answer to yet, and that's -- say you have a couple going out to dinner, and they tell the baby-sitter, well, the children have to do chores, you know, you decide which ones."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they do not rely on RFRA for the moral exemption. They claim authority under 300gg-13, under the ACA's women's health amendment, for the moral exemption."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is, as you know, the statute says that they have to provide additional preventive care as provided for in comprehensive guidelines supported by the Health Resources and Services Administration. Well, read that and you have at least some ambiguity. So my question is really, given your argument and given what may well be ambiguity at least in the statute, why didn't you make the argument, it's arbitrary, capricious, abuse of discretion? You're saying it's too broad, you're saying it'll hurt women, you -- you -- you know, you -- you point out that it'll raise healthcare costs and a whole lot of things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Fischer, you say that the Affordable Care Act does not allow the government to make any exceptions to the contraceptive mandate to accommodate religious objections."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0003-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They don't have to say specifically we have this objection. We are not providing coverage."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I guess the question is, why should there be any real difference between those two?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Okay. So I'm right in saying that this really does depend on whether the good cause requirement was satisfied in the first place?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what -- what do we do about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General FRANCISCO",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "212ca54b744692a869a70a4fbea812bce1305d5d6af3fe808085d161611061d3",
      "evidence_id": "ev-212ca54b7446-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 99,
        "start": 99
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Although RFRA both authorizes and requires these exemptions, at the very least, they're justified under Section 13(a)(4)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-19-431",
      "confidence": 0.0,
